    "https://ogp.me/ns#title": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Carl Ludwig Hübsch: Musique + Discussion | Le Vivier"
      }
    ],
    "https://ogp.me/ns#description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "This performance-conference will offer the public an opportunity to discover the musical universe of Carl Ludwig Hübsch, an artist who doesn't hesitate to sing, play the tuba, and share his creative process with the audience.Carl Ludwig Hübsch is a renowned composer and tuba player, co-founder and composer of the Multiple Joy[ce] Orchestra. His work explores the links between composition and improvisation, two practices that he considers complementary and sources of mutual enrichment.In residence in Quebec in March and April 2025, as part of an exchange and workshops between Quebec and Dresden, he will present \"Cartographie - Origines\", an ambitious research and creation project that will lead him to meet Quebec musicians passionate about new and improvised music.A presentation by Productions SuperMusique, in partnership with Le Vivier, the Goethe-Institut and the CALQ.This program is made possible thanks to the collaboration of HELLERAU - European Center for the Arts Dresden, Goethe-Institut Montréal, Le Vivier - Carrefour des musiques nouvelles, and the Quebec Office in Berlin"
      }
    ],
