      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "J.Zhu is a composer, artist, and carillonneur. Her work is visual and aural, operating on an expansive definition of score, striving for the unexpected obvious and expressive absurd.\r\n\r\nShe entangles various media, from mural painting and sculpture to performance and video, and collaborates with artists from different fields to create experimental chamber experiences. &nbsp;She has activated living rooms, concert halls, art galleries, bell towers, caves, copses, and once made a tiny house for just one harpsichordist’s body and the keyboard.\r\n\r\nHer scores range from hair cast in clear..."
      }
    ],
    "@type": [
      "http://schema.org/Person"
    ]
  },
