    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Kristie Ibrahim began her musical education at the age of 4 and&nbsp; she continued her training at Dalhousie University where she studied with Jim Faraday, and completed an apprenticeship with Symphony Nova Scotia.&nbsp; \r\n\r\nNext, she moved to New Zealand, where she worked with percussion ensemble Strike, with whom she discovered a passion for the theatrical dimension of performing.&nbsp; She also played with the New Zealand Symphony Orchestra, the Auckland Philharmonia, and the Wellington Sinfonia as well as with ensembles Stroma and Verona.\r\n\r\nUpon her return to Canada, she moved to..."
      }
    ],
