    ],
    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "La porte vers les sirènes"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/identifier": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "https://levivier.ca/en/le-vivier/repertoire/la-porte-vers-les-sirenes"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/abstract": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Siren.\r\nQuestions.\r\nIntrospection.&nbsp;\r\nWho are they?\r\nDiscovery.\r\nA door.&nbsp;\r\nThe door.\r\nThe door that binds.\r\nThe door that knows.\r\nThe door that shouts.\r\nShould it be opened?\r\nWill it open?&nbsp;\r\nWould you open it?\r\n\r\nThe door is also a tribute to Jean-François Laporte and his instrument the mermaid organ.&nbsp;\r\n\r\nI first heard a mermaid played as a musical instrument in 2001, during Danielle Palardy Roger's Port Symphony. She used techniques developed by Jean-François Laporte. I fell in love with this instrument and decided at that moment that one day I would compose for..."
      }
    ],
    "@type": [
      "http://schema.org/MusicComposition"
    ]
  },
