    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Born in Rouyn-Noranda (Québec), Simon Martin (1981-) is a composer and producer of contemporary concert music. As the founding director of Projections libérantes (2011), he has completed four productions to this day. Musique d’art pour trompette, cor, trombone, euphonium et électronique, an international coproduction between Projections libérantes and l’Ensemble Musikfabrik, will be premiered in 2021.\r\n\r\nFollowing in the footsteps of American composers Harry Partch, La Monte Young and James Tenney, Martin’s music increasingly focuses on just intonation. The narrative of his..."
      }
    ],
