    ],
    "http://schema.org/familyName": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Gerenabarrena"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Zuriñe F. Gerenabarrena (1965) studied music composition in Vitoria-Gasteiz with Carmelo Bernaola at the J. Guridi Conservatory, and with Franco Donatoni at the Scuola Civica in Milan. She is a versatile composer, who has worked as an orchestrator for movies and has many works ranging between orders for soloists, symphony orchestra, theater, dance, animation, electroacoustics and multidisciplinary projects. She has been invited to several international meetings. She also worked as a resident artist in Tokyo Wonder Site (Japan); VICC, Visby (Sweden); USF/Verfet, Bergen (Norway); Laboratorio..."
      }
    ],
    "@type": [
      "http://schema.org/Person"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "_:g12106200",
    "http://schema.org/url": [
      {
        "@id": "https://levivier.ca/en/le-vivier/repertoire/quantum-statistical-zero-knowledge"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/datePublished": [
      {
        "@type": "http://schema.org/Date",
        "@value": "2021"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/composer": [
      {
        "@id": "_:g12106220"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Quantum Statistical Zero-Knowledge"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/identifier": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "https://levivier.ca/en/le-vivier/repertoire/quantum-statistical-zero-knowledge"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/abstract": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "“Quantum physics teaches us that we can simultaneously exist in many places, under certain conditions.”\r\nAmit Ray, Quantum Computing Algorithms for Artificial Intelligence\r\n\r\n“Avec assez de temps, tout peut arriver, statistiquement.”\r\nElisabeth Vonarburg, Chronique du Pays des Mères\r\n\r\n“Entre ce qui a eu lieu et ce qui n’a pas eu lieu, il n’y a pas plus de différence qu’entre plus zéro et moins zéro.”\r\nAmélie Nothomb, Péplum\r\n\r\n“Information is not knowledge. The only source of knowledge is experience.”\r\nCitation faussement attribuée à Albert..."
      }
    ],
    "@type": [
      "http://schema.org/MusicComposition"
    ]
  },
