    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Born in 1982, Didier Rotella has studied piano and composition at the Conservatories of Lyon and Paris, at IRCAM, and at Ecole Normale Alfred Cortot with Frédéric Durieux, Edith Canat de Chizy, Anne Queffélec, Françoise Thinat, Hector Parrà, André Gorog...\r\n\r\nHis recent works testify to a research of the instrumental gesture as primacy to the organization of the musical discourse whether in the relation musician-electronics or in his acoustic pieces, while his profession of interpreter brings him from chamber music to solo repertoire through many creations, alone or in contemporary..."
      }
