    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Antoine Mailloux first started learning the trumpet at age eleven at the Escale secondary school in Asbestos, Quebec.\r\nMotivated by his interest in music, he first spent summers practicing and touring with the local drum and bugle corps Les Stentors, as a mellophone player. After obtaining a diploma in Classical Trumpet Performance at the Cégep de Saint-Laurent with Frédéric Gagnon, Antoine auditioned for admittance to the Conservatoire de musique de Montréal, aiming to study there with the renowned Shawinigan-based trumpeter Benjamin Raymond.Since the beginning of his studies with Mr...."
      }
    ],
