    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Laurent Durupt is gratuated in piano, chamber music, analysis, counterpoint, improvisation and composition at the CNSM Conservatoire National Superieur de Paris. He won several prizes at piano competitions (Pordenone, Grosseto), Chamber Music competition (Krakovia, Paris) and composition prizes (Tenso Young Composer Award). His principal teachers were Hugues Leclere, Pascal Devoyon, Bruno Rigutto, Nicholas Angelich and Henri Barda for the piano, Frédéric Durieux, Luis Naon, Allain Gaussin and Philippe Leroux for composition. He was resident to academy of Royaumont «Voix Nouvelles» in..."
      }
