    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Laura Doyle Péan, born in Quebec City in 1999, is a poet and activist of Haitian-Quebec origin.\r\nLaura Doyle Péan is the daughter of Haitian writer, broadcaster and journalist Stanley Péan, himself a descendant of poet Oswald Durand1. She grew up in Quebec City where she was born in 1999. As a teenager, she worked as a bookseller for a few years.\r\nIn 2019, she joined the feminist art collective Les Allumeuses.\r\n"
      }
    ],
