        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Davidson"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Robert Davidson’s music is most often focused on telling stories, especially using recorded speech and its inherent melody, but also through using aspects of many genres freely combined. His quintet Topology is very interested in collaborating without worrying about style boundaries. Such an attitude attracted him to study with Terry Riley before spending a year in India studying the rich dance-drama traditions of Kerala.\r\n\r\nRobert also tours widely as a bassist and as a lecturer. He teaches at the University of Queensland, after years as an orchestral bassist. He writes a lot of music..."
      }
    ],
    "@type": [
      "http://schema.org/Person"
    ]
  },
