      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/abstract": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Viola and saxophone quartet\r\nAs in many chamber music works by Georges Aperghis, in Crosswind language comes into play. In the conversations of the performers, speaking in a gibberish invented by Aperghis, there are occasional sparks of speech that can be understood: the essence of music here is to be a foreign language..\r\n\r\n&nbsp;At the time when Aperghis was writing Crosswind, he was interested in the writings of the behavioural researcher Conrad Lorenz, and based on that work he began closely studying animalistic behaviour among musicians. “This is no longer a question of similarity..."
      }
    ],
    "@type": [
      "http://schema.org/MusicComposition"
    ]
  },
