        "@value": "Scheuer"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Benjamin Scheuer’s music is all about sensuality and humor. Both staged and concert pieces contain theatrical elements and often evoke an atmosphere of darkly colored playfulness. In his works found objects from daily live are frequently being presented on stage — either live or sampled: Scheuer nevertheless doesn’t consider himself to be a composer of electronic music but rather focuses on a world of “live-electrics” in which sounds are produced with the easiest and most economic means possible. His main interest is the human being playing music with its individual characteristic..."
      }
    ],
    "@type": [
      "http://schema.org/Person"
    ]
  },
