    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Spationautes II"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/identifier": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "https://levivier.ca/en/le-vivier/repertoire/spationautes-ii"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/abstract": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Commissioned by SuperMusique, for ensemble of musicians-improvisers, spatialized electroacoustic tape* and interactive projections\r\n\r\nSpationautes is initially a graphic work, an imaginary world in five dimensions that I created in the form of drawings. Each dimension represents a distinct cosmological point of view: cosmos, ether, landscape, jungle and hypogeum (the latter being a somewhat strange microscopic underground world). The drawings of these five parallel 'space-times' serve as a canvas, orchestration and inspiration for the musical improvisation.&nbsp;\r\nAccompanied by..."
      }
    ],
    "@type": [
      "http://schema.org/MusicComposition"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "_:g13882560",
    "http://schema.org/url": [
      {
        "@id": "https://levivier.ca/en/le-vivier/repertoire/le-trace-de-londe"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/datePublished": [
      {
        "@type": "http://schema.org/Date",
        "@value": "2023"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Le tracé de l’onde"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/identifier": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "https://levivier.ca/en/le-vivier/repertoire/le-trace-de-londe"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/abstract": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Commissioned by SuperMusique, with support from the Canada Council for the Arts\r\n\r\nA work that is part of the 'Living Structures' series, a research project that Linda has been working on since 2017, namely how to interpret data from the analysis of complex sounds to create graphic images of them. In 2018 she created a unique tool, Ocular Scores, in close collaboration with Joseph Browne, a tool that has continued to evolve since.\r\n&nbsp;\r\nIn this new work, the three instrumental groups are spatially separated to create three distinct voices, three timbres, three textures that visually..."
      }
    ],
    "@type": [
      "http://schema.org/MusicComposition"
    ]
  },
