    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "\r\n\"Legend has it that one day Pythagoras was amazed by the sounds that blacksmiths made when they struck their pieces of metal [...]. When he returned home, the Greek thinker hastened to explore sound and invent new instruments.\"\r\n\r\n\r\nIn this co-creation by Rachel Warr (Dotted Line Theatre) and Benjamin Oliver, performed by the musicians of Paramirabo, our hero, the modern-day Pythagoras, invites children aged 3 to 12 (but also adults) to follow him in his surreal, amusing and even danceable experiments. \r\n"
      }
    ]
