  {
    "@id": "_:g14600160",
    "http://schema.org/url": [
      {
        "@id": "https://levivier.ca/en/le-vivier/repertoire/axe-rouge-ii"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/datePublished": [
      {
        "@type": "http://schema.org/Date",
        "@value": "2007"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Axe Rouge II"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/identifier": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "https://levivier.ca/en/le-vivier/repertoire/axe-rouge-ii"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/abstract": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "AXE ROUGE II was commissioned by INA/GRM and is part of a series of pieces with the same title, numbered I to V. In five movements linked by transitions, passages or frames, AXE ROUGE II expresses itself in rhythms and sound colours derived for the most part from unusual objects, such as beer cans, the sounds of objects as well as various recycled sound fragments which have found their place here. The instrumental sounds are integrated into the electroacoustic sound universe, bringing their own colours and expressions. \r\n"
      }
    ],
    "@type": [
      "http://schema.org/MusicComposition"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "_:g14600200",
    "http://schema.org/url": [
      {
        "@id": "https://levivier.ca/en/le-vivier/repertoire/instrumental-interaction-ii"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/datePublished": [
      {
        "@type": "http://schema.org/Date",
        "@value": "2023"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Instrumental Interaction II"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/identifier": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "https://levivier.ca/en/le-vivier/repertoire/instrumental-interaction-ii"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/abstract": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "\"Instrumental Interaction II explores the sonic and gestural relationships between the Karlax, a clarinet-like MIDI controller with an undefined identity, and the tenor saxophone, an agile, variegated and powerful instrument. A piece that focuses on the importance of gesture in musical interpretation but also on the kinetic evocation carried by the music itself around two communicating vessels/instruments.\r\n\r\nBenjamin Lavastre is currently a PhD candidate at McGill University and a member of CIRMMT. The creation of his piece tonight is part of his ongoing doctoral research on this digital..."
      }
    ],
    "@type": [
      "http://schema.org/MusicComposition"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "_:g14600240",
    "http://schema.org/url": [
      {
        "@id": "https://levivier.ca/en/le-vivier/repertoire/extraction-brouille-de-noir"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/datePublished": [
      {
        "@type": "http://schema.org/Date",
        "@value": "2023"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Extraction - brouillé de noir"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/identifier": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "https://levivier.ca/en/le-vivier/repertoire/extraction-brouille-de-noir"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/abstract": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Extraction\r\nD'un monde sans raison\r\nJe regarde au loin\r\nSans y voir de point.\r\nVive passion\r\nEteinte à l'unisson\r\nCafé froid,\r\nJe le bois.\r\nRéflexion\r\nFaite en portion\r\nDualité reignant\r\nFace à l'amour fainéant...\r\nExctinction\r\nD'un feu sans nation\r\nEtouffant mon monde\r\nTel un boa immonde\r\nDisparition\r\nDu « je », « moi », « surmoi »\r\nC'est sorti en fractions :\r\nExtraction\r\n\r\nAlithéa R.I.P.(oll)\r\n&nbsp;\r\n\r\n&nbsp;\r\n"
      }
    ],
    "@type": [
      "http://schema.org/MusicComposition"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "_:g14600280",
    "http://schema.org/url": [
      {
        "@id": "https://levivier.ca/en/le-vivier/repertoire/que-par-un-etre-dont-le-coeur-bat"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/datePublished": [
      {
        "@type": "http://schema.org/Date",
        "@value": "2023"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "“...que par un être dont le coeur bat…”"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/identifier": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "https://levivier.ca/en/le-vivier/repertoire/que-par-un-etre-dont-le-coeur-bat"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/abstract": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "'... que par un être dont le coeur bat...' focuses on the evolution of materials over time and space, not from a process perspective, but rather from a dialectical perspective: how one can influence the other, vertically as well as horizontally and transversally.&nbsp;\r\n\r\nBased on a dynamic and articulated rhetoric, this piece proposes a rhythmic scenario that exploits the contrasts between simple and eloquent materials, all of which carry ideas that are both fragile and powerful. At times complementary and at others contradictory, the materials are used to articulate a virtuoso sound..."
      }
    ],
    "@type": [
      "http://schema.org/MusicComposition"
    ]
  },
