  {
    "@id": "_:g15138640",
    "http://schema.org/url": [
      {
        "@id": "https://levivier.ca/fr/le-vivier/repertoire/estatuas"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/datePublished": [
      {
        "@type": "http://schema.org/Date",
        "@value": "2023"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Estatuas"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/identifier": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "https://levivier.ca/fr/le-vivier/repertoire/estatuas"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/abstract": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "\r\nI do not know the names of the statues, but I know that marble has frozen their lives, and that there is something striking from within.\" Esther Ramondelli, De heridas y luciérnagas\r\n\r\n\r\nWhat if we were all like statues locked inside marble, preserving our lives but depriving ourselves of the freedom to express? What if this marble took the name of fear, illness, or simply powerlessness? I tried to imagine what strikes us from the inside, what is alive and seeks a crack to escape. Thus, a fleeting melodic line is born from within. It awakens the most organic sounds, transforming into..."
      }
    ],
    "@type": [
      "http://schema.org/MusicComposition"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "_:g15138680",
    "http://schema.org/url": [
      {
        "@id": "https://levivier.ca/fr/le-vivier/repertoire/when-jessica-smile"
