  {
    "@id": "_:g15138840",
    "http://schema.org/url": [
      {
        "@id": "https://levivier.ca/en/le-vivier/repertoire/lo-azul-traves-de-un-hueco"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Lo azul a traves de un hueco"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/identifier": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "https://levivier.ca/en/le-vivier/repertoire/lo-azul-traves-de-un-hueco"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/abstract": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "\r\n“Composing is a leap, and a sloppy one, into the void. It is not the expansive abyss of immensity. It is the impudent abyss of the fall. Personally, I find it stimulating to write music thinking about sound materials and not about aesthetics or procedures that can be competed for by elites. I try to generate aesthetic approaches as a result and not as a starting point. Sometimes I believe that the work of a composer is his life itself, a journey, which he did not set out to be. Although only sometimes I think so…”\r\n\r\n\r\nLo Azul a travel de un hueco was conceived rather as a..."
      }
    ],
    "@type": [
      "http://schema.org/MusicComposition"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "_:g15138880",
    "http://schema.org/url": [
      {
        "@id": "https://levivier.ca/en/le-vivier/repertoire/steeped"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/datePublished": [
      {
        "@type": "http://schema.org/Date",
        "@value": "2023"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Steeped"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/identifier": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "https://levivier.ca/en/le-vivier/repertoire/steeped"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/abstract": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "I’ve had the pleasure of knowing Krystina and Juan Sebastian, of Stick &amp; Bow, for a decade. We have worked together in many capacities and configurations – on my music and that of others – in dramatic live performances, intense recording sessions, and even music for silent film. Steeped is my first work for Stick &amp; Bow as a duo, and I was inspired by something that seems impossible: Can I create a piece in which the marimba and cello, two instruments that could not be more different from each other, are melded into one organism, one complicated sound world in which both..."
      }
    ],
    "@type": [
      "http://schema.org/MusicComposition"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "_:g15138920",
    "http://schema.org/url": [
      {
        "@id": "https://levivier.ca/en/le-vivier/repertoire/dialogos-imaginarios"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/datePublished": [
      {
        "@type": "http://schema.org/Date",
        "@value": "2023"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Dialogos imaginarios "
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/identifier": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "https://levivier.ca/en/le-vivier/repertoire/dialogos-imaginarios"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/abstract": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "In the prologue of \"El libro de los seres imaginarios,\" Jorge L. Borges declares that \"the name of this book would justify the inclusion of Prince Hamlet, the point, the line... the hypercube, all generic words... and perhaps, each one of us and divinity. In short, almost the universe.\" Imagination may be the most powerful weapon at our disposal, one that can defy gods and time in an uneven but unwavering struggle. We, humans, have used it to create, destroy, affirm, and deny; its very multiplication - as if Proteus inhabited each of us - is the origin of all things, as Borges..."
      }
    ],
    "@type": [
      "http://schema.org/MusicComposition"
    ]
  },
