    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "INFORMATION: Montréal Oct. 1970"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/identifier": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "https://levivier.ca/en/le-vivier/repertoire/information-montreal-oct-1970"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/abstract": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "ABOUT THE OPERA\r\nBased in part on real events and historical figures, the action of the opera takes place in Montreal in October 1970. The plot focuses on the relationship between two journalists: a young anglophone named Mary Vance, and the older, seasoned francophone reporter Sylvain Leclerc. The two reporters end up collaborating closely on coverage of the kidnapping of James Cross by the FLQ. Parallel to the events of the October Crisis, Mary is living her own personal crisis, as she is seeking to terminate an unwanted pregnancy, which was illegal in 1970.\r\n\r\n\r\n“There is a recurrent..."
      }
    ],
    "@type": [
      "http://schema.org/MusicComposition"
    ]
  },
