        "@value": "https://levivier.ca/en/concert/2024-25-season/le-week-end-rouge"
      }
    ],
    "https://ogp.me/ns#title": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Le week-end rouge | Le Vivier"
      }
    ],
    "https://ogp.me/ns#description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Le Week-end Rouge is a commemoration in song and music of a social drama that marked the residents of Montreal's Centre-Sud district 50 years ago, through a two-movement piece for choir, seven soloists, oboe, euphonium, organ, percussion and invented string instruments. The concert highlights the social and historical aspects of this event. The intention is in no way denunciatory, but rather a poetic illustration, in song and music, of the need for rapprochement that people feel in the context of disasters or bad weather. 7:30 p.m. - Parc Pierre-Bourgault, rue Alexandre-DeSèveFirst part of the outdoor concert, at Parc Pierre-Bourgault8 p.m. - Église du Sacré-Cœur-de-Jésus, rue OntarioFor the second part of the concert, the public is invited to join us at the Église du Sacré-Cœur-de-Jésus, located on Ontario Street between Plessis and Alexandre-DeSève."
      }
    ],
