  {
    "@id": "_:g16984440",
    "http://schema.org/url": [
      {
        "@id": "https://levivier.ca/en/le-vivier/repertoire/ne-teveilles-pas-de-ton-reve"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/datePublished": [
      {
        "@type": "http://schema.org/Date",
        "@value": "2025"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": " ...ne t'éveilles pas de ton rêve"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/identifier": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "https://levivier.ca/en/le-vivier/repertoire/ne-teveilles-pas-de-ton-reve"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/abstract": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "A sad, clean, old-fashioned apartment perched atop a modern building. A party, guests, small talk—boredom revealing its cracks in every detail. The apartment empties. I find myself in the corner of a room. A small woman stands before me, blocking my path. Impatient, I crumple her up. Disgusted by my violent gesture, I make a decision: “It’s time to end this dream—I’ll jump out the window, and the fall will wake me.” I leap through the glass, but instead of falling, I soar above the city. I fly for a long time, crossing the boundary between the city and “the other world.”This..."
      }
    ],
    "@type": [
      "http://schema.org/MusicComposition"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "_:g16984480",
    "http://schema.org/url": [
      {
        "@id": "https://levivier.ca/en/le-vivier/repertoire/states-intermeshing"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/datePublished": [
      {
        "@type": "http://schema.org/Date",
        "@value": "2025"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "States of Intermeshing"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/identifier": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "https://levivier.ca/en/le-vivier/repertoire/states-intermeshing"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/abstract": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "In recent years, my interest in elements surrounding eschatological forces has deepened. By examining the historical and social roots of such movements, one quickly sees the undeniable links between the foundations of global colonization and the capitalist world as we know it today, and apocalyptic discourses. These narratives have continuously—and still—disadvantaged marginalized communities, particularly Afro-diasporic ones. States of Intermeshing, viii. what is past is prologue thus explores the intrinsic relationship between the dehumanization of Black communities and apocalyptic..."
      }
    ],
    "@type": [
      "http://schema.org/MusicComposition"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "_:g16984520",
    "http://schema.org/url": [
      {
        "@id": "https://levivier.ca/en/le-vivier/repertoire/swim-sharks-walk-dragons"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/datePublished": [
      {
        "@type": "http://schema.org/Date",
        "@value": "2025"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Swim with the sharks, walk with the dragons"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/identifier": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "https://levivier.ca/en/le-vivier/repertoire/swim-sharks-walk-dragons"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/abstract": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "The title of the piece relates two almost opposite ways of conceiving life.The first part comes from Harvey Mackay's book Swim with the Sharks Without Being Eaten Alive, a bestseller published in 1988, whose spirit is representative of the capitalism of the last decades. The author proposes a series of effective strategies for business and negotiation, always with the aim of succeeding and winning over opponents, no matter what happens. As for the second part, Marcher avec les dragons is a French adaptation of anthropologist Tim Ingold’s writings and thinking, developed from his field..."
      }
    ],
    "@type": [
      "http://schema.org/MusicComposition"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "_:g16984560",
    "http://schema.org/url": [
